{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788059229842066001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"immense-feedable-weevil","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":1,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"b45989d21e7d8b033fa01b709a92e63798925fde30ccba416da883fd013014a1","event_uuid":"2116e582-cc91-4209-a168-8d2a8868d1c0","position":{"commit_sha":"fe8da24ffa312400c36004199f28c63c00823402","position":"1788056673183653005-2116e582-cc91-4209-a168-8d2a8868d1c0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788056673183653005,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## Finding (audit of epic 3405-c0b7)\n**Site:** `src/rebar/_reads.py:99` sets `err.error_code = \"pinned_ticket_read_failed\"`, returned verbatim by `error_code_for` branch 5 (the `exc.error_code` passthrough). But `pinned_ticket_read_failed` is NOT a member of `KNOWN_ERROR_CODES` (`src/rebar/_errors.py:48-66`).\n\n**Problem:** the code itself is descriptive (NOT misleading). The defect is a vocabulary-completeness gap: `error_code_for`'s own docstring says it \"Returns a stable vocabulary code (one of KNOWN_ERROR_CODES)\", but this passthrough emits a code outside that set. Any consumer that validates the returned code against `KNOWN_ERROR_CODES` (the documented contract) would reject a legitimately-emitted code, or fall back to treating it as unknown.\n\n**Observable vs latent:** OBSERVABLE — emitted on the pinned-ticket read failure path; reaches the MCP envelope guard and the CLI reader envelope.\n\n**Proposed fix — READY-TO-FIX (reuse existing, no design decision):** add `\"pinned_ticket_read_failed\"` to the `KNOWN_ERROR_CODES` frozenset so the emitted vocabulary and the declared vocabulary agree. (Alternatively, add a contract test that asserts every `err.error_code` string assigned in the tree is a member of `KNOWN_ERROR_CODES` — see the epic's prevention recommendation.) Low priority; not misleading, but it violates the stated vocabulary contract.\n\n**caused_by / class:** vocabulary drift, not the `llm_unavailable` pattern.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","3405-c0b7-0436-4b46"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"3405-c0b7-0436-4b46","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["error-taxonomy","ready-to-fix"],"ticket_id":"0aee-a70d-045b-48a1","ticket_type":"bug","title":"pinned_ticket_read_failed is emitted but absent from KNOWN_ERROR_CODES (vocabulary-contract gap)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["2116e582-cc91-4209-a168-8d2a8868d1c0"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788059229842066001,"uuid":"f26b42b7-b014-4a08-944f-fc3b8bef4c7b"}